Author: JBailes <jbailes@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 22 20:33:07 2026 +0000

    separate catalog vendor identity from wire provider
    
    agent_t.provider names the WIRE SHAPE aimee speaks. It was also being used as
    the key for model_capability_get(), so a third-party vendor served over another
    vendor's API resolved nothing. MiniMax and Kimi are registered provider=
    "anthropic" (they expose Anthropic-compatible endpoints) while models.dev keys
    them "minimax"/"moonshotai", so every capability lookup missed and fell through
    to the heuristic's anthropic branch, which matches no claude-* prefix.
    
    Live consequences, all fixed here:
    
    - Both models lost MODEL_CAP_REASONING, so agent_config.c derived the SHORT
      per-call timeout for them. The comment at that site names the symptom: slow
      multi-minute completions cut off and retried as spurious read failures.
    - MiniMax-M3 resolved a 200000 context window from a stale bare "minimax"
      prefix entry against a true 1000000 - a 5x understatement on the longest
      context model in the fleet.
    - kimi-k2.7-code resolved 0 (no prefix entry at all), and the min_context gate
      guarded with `effective_ctx > 0`, so an unknown window PASSED for arbitrarily
      large prompts. That failure looked like success.
    
    Add agent_t.catalog_provider, derived at load from the endpoint host (never a
    single model version - the existing openai->minimax remap keyed on the literal
    "MiniMax-M2" and broke the moment M3 shipped). provider is left untouched
    because it drives three live behaviors: the anthropic-version header, the
    x-api-key auth coercion, and the credential env-var set. Only an operator
    supplied catalog_provider re-serializes, so a save never freezes a derived
    guess into config.
    
    Route the four capability-lookup call sites through agent_catalog_provider().
    Make an unknown context window fail the min_context gate rather than pass it,
    mirroring delegate_routing.c's CLI-adapter fallback first so tmux-backed agents
    that carry no resolvable model are not stranded.
    
    Add a moonshotai heuristic branch: without it a "moonshotai" catalog identity
    falls through with flags == 0 on a cold models.dev cache, which is strictly
    worse than the wrong "anthropic" identity it replaces.
    
    Tests assert the vendor/wire split, explicit-vs-derived round trip, the
    corrected context windows, that zero context no longer satisfies min_context,
    and the end-to-end payoff that both agents now resolve REASONING and receive
    AGENT_REASONING_TIMEOUT_MS.
    
    No routing policy change: model_meta_capability_routing still defaults off, so
    agent_route() behavior is unchanged.

